            "explanation": "The change modifies line 39 to ensure that if 'options' is undefined or null, it is defaulted to an empty object before being cloned via JSON. Previously, if 'options' was undefined, JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(options)) would throw an error. This fix prevents that error and properly initializes new RedisClient instances without requiring options.",
            "suggestion": "Use 'options = JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(options || {}))' instead of 'options = JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(options))' in RedisClient constructor."
